[{"id":32113194403,"node_id":"LE_lADOEFLz888AAAABT_rK788AAAAHehh1ow","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/events/32113194403","actor":{"login":"barthdvs","id":102857359,"node_id":"U_kgDOBiF6jw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102857359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs","html_url":"https://github.com/barthdvs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-29T20:45:07Z","label":{"name":"bug","color":"d73a4a"},"intent":null,"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":32113322807,"node_id":"SE_lADOEFLz888AAAABT_rK788AAAAHehprNw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/events/32113322807","actor":{"login":"barthdvs","id":102857359,"node_id":"U_kgDOBiF6jw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102857359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs","html_url":"https://github.com/barthdvs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-29T20:47:07Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/5898633485","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/3512#issuecomment-5898633485","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3512","id":5898633485,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz888AAAABX5YBDQ","user":{"login":"barthdvs","id":102857359,"node_id":"U_kgDOBiF6jw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102857359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs","html_url":"https://github.com/barthdvs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T20:51:39Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T20:51:39Z","body":"Follow-up with measurements. We reproduced the problem offline on a copy of the database and measured each step of the upgrade path with a real client.\n\n**Protocol**: database restored from a dump taken on 0.26.1, one Tailscale 1.102.5 client registered under the subnet router's user, its 60 routes advertised and approved, then the client restarted with its state. The timer stops when the client is `Running` and has received its peers. Same machine for all runs, no reverse proxy, no other client.\n\n**First netmap for a node with 946 peers**\n\n| Version | First netmap | headscale CPU time | Registering a node |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.26.1 | 2.6 s | 0.1 s | 2.4 s |\n| 0.27.1 | 10.3–11.3 s | 10–12 s | 20.0 s |\n| 0.28.0 | 10.3–15.4 s | 11–16 s | 18.8–24.1 s |\n| 0.29.4 | 82.8–86.1 s | 90–92 s | 11.9 s |\n\nOn 0.29.4, after a second restart of the client, the netmap was **never delivered within 600 s** (2 runs out of 2), with `map response long-poll timed out!` every 120 s.\n\n**This is not a deadlock or an endless loop.** Goroutine dumps taken every 25 s during the failing case show one worker computing in `resolveUser` / `AppendToIPSet`, and `headscale_mapresponse_generated_total` keeps increasing slowly. The computation is simply too slow, and the work started for a request that the client has already given up on (after 120 s) is not cancelled, so the queue for that node never drains.\n\n**Where the time goes** (CPU profiles)\n\n| Case | Hot path | Share |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0.29.4, netmap of the router | `generateMapResponse → buildTailPeers → TailNode → RoutesForPeer → ViaRoutesForPeer → Group.Resolve → Username.resolve → resolveUser` | 90 % |\n| 0.29.4, registering a node | `snapshotFromNodes → BuildPeerMap` | 59 % |\n| 0.28.0, netmap of the router | `snapshotFromNodes → BuildPeerMap` | 77 % |\n\n**Control experiment**: with an allow-all policy on 0.29.4, the same node gets its netmap in 2.8–7.2 s with 1026 peers. The cost comes from resolving the policy, not from the size of the netmap.\n\n**Workarounds measured on 0.29.4** (no code change)\n\n| Change | First netmap | After restart | Peers |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| none | 86.1 s | fails at 600 s | 946 |\n| `tuning` (`node_store_batch_size=1000`, `node_store_batch_timeout=5000ms`, `batch_change_delay=10s`, `batcher_workers=4`) and `node.routes.ha.probe_interval: 0s` | 98.3 s | fails at 600 s | 946 |\n| router converted to a tagged node | 88.8 s | not measured | 946 |\n| usernames matching no user removed from groups | 43.9 s | 60.9 s | 946 |\n| 477 stale nodes deleted (expired, or offline for more than 90 days) | 36.0 s | 44.8 s | 514 |\n| `acls` rewritten as native `grants`, one grant per rule (52 instead of 341) | 19.4 s | 14.2 s | 946 |\n| `grants` and unmatched usernames removed | 12.7 s | 12.6 s | 946 |\n| `grants`, unmatched usernames removed, stale nodes deleted | 9.0 s | 4.6 s, 8.7 s | 514 |\n\nWith the last combination and 12 clients restarted together with headscale (2 routers, 10 regular clients): regular clients get their netmap in 7.9–9.4 s, routers in 12.6 s and 12.9 s.\n\nThe `grants` rewrite is equivalent: the compiled filter from `/debug/filter` is identical to the one produced by the original `acls` policy, and the router keeps its 946 peers. All variants pass `headscale policy check` on 0.29.4.\n\n**Takeaways**\n\n- Offline, stale and expired nodes still count as peers, so they cost as much as online ones.\n- Writing the same rules as `acls` costs about 4 times more than writing them as `grants`, because `aclToGrants` emits one grant per destination and the sources are resolved again for each of them.\n- An early return in `ViaRoutesForPeer` when the policy has no `via` grant should bring 0.29 back to the 0.28 numbers for policies like ours.\n\nCorrection to the description above: the 96 s figure came from a log line read during an earlier run; with the protocol described here the first netmap takes 82.8–86.1 s.\n\nPossibly related: #3417, #3108, #3501, #3156.\n\nWe can run more measurements on this copy of the database, or test a patch, if that is useful.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/5898633485/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"barthdvs","id":102857359,"node_id":"U_kgDOBiF6jw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102857359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs","html_url":"https://github.com/barthdvs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barthdvs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":32170561556,"node_id":"LE_lADOEFLz888AAAABT_rK788AAAAHfYPQFA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/events/32170561556","actor":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users